.TH "iSCSI SCST Target Daemon" 8 "May 2007" Linux "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
iscsi-scstd \- iSCSI SCST Target Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iscsi-scstd
.RB [\| \-c
.IR configfile \|]
.RB [\| \-d
.IR debuglevel \|]
.RB [\| \-f \|]
.RB [\| \-g
.IR GID \|]
.RB [\| \-h \|]
.RB [\| \-a
.IR address \|]
.RB [\| \-p
.IR port \|]
.RB [\| \-u
.IR UID \|]
.RB [\| \-v \|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B iscsi-scstd
program implements the user-space control and login part of the iSCSI-SCST
target. It must run while the kernel iSCSI target is in use.
.PP
The legacy iscsi-scstd.conf format is optional. Use scstadmin and
/etc/scst.conf for new persistent configurations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c\  filename ,\ \-\-config= filename
Read the legacy configuration from
.IR filename .
If this option is omitted,
.I /etc/iscsi-scstd.conf
is read when it exists.
.TP
.BI \-d\  debuglevel ,\ \-\-debug= debuglevel
Set the debug verbosity. In daemon mode messages are sent through
.BR syslog (3);
in foreground mode they are written to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-f,\  \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground instead of forking into the background.
.TP
.BI \-g\  GID ,\ \-\-gid= GID
Specify running group id, default is current gid.
.TP
.BI \-a\  address\ ... ,\ \-\-address= address\ ...
Listen only on the specified local addresses instead of all local addresses.
Pass multiple addresses as one quoted, space-separated argument.
.TP
.BI \-p\  port ,\ \-\-port= port
Specify on which port the server should listen, default is 3260.
.TP
.BI \-h,\  \-\-help
Display help message on command line options.
.TP
.BI \-u\  UID ,\ \-\-uid= UID
Specify running user id, default is current uid.
.TP
.BI \-v,\  \-\-version
Display the program version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/iscsi-scstd.conf
The optional legacy configuration file. See
.BR iscsi-scstd.conf (5)
for further details.
.TP
.I /run/iscsi-scstd.pid
The process ID file created in daemon mode.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
In daemon mode, messages are sent through
.BR syslog (3).
With
.BR \-f ,
messages are written to standard error. The debug level controls additional
diagnostic output. Kernel data-path messages are reported separately through
the kernel log.
.SH SECURITY
By default, iscsi-scstd listens on all local addresses on port 3260. Restrict
the listening addresses and configure authentication and initiator access
controls before enabling a target on an untrusted network.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Header and data digests are not implemented for discovery sessions.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR iscsi-scstd.conf (5)
